-- title:
--   Places above a finite j-value as ℚ̄-points of the coordinate ring
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and write $\bar F_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the subextension of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $N$; let $\bar\jmath =$ `jBar N` be the element of $\bar F_N$ given by the $q$-expansion of the $j$-function. Let $j_0 \in \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, and assume that every place of $\bar F_N$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a proper valuation subring of $\bar F_N$ containing $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and which is a principal ideal ring — has degree one, i.e. its residue field has $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-dimension $1$. Let $A_N$ denote the integral closure of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}[\bar\jmath] =$ `Algebra.adjoin (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) {jBar N}` in $\bar F_N$. Then the type of bijections between the set of places $v$ of $\bar F_N$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\operatorname{ord}_v(\bar\jmath - j_0) > 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_v$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation, and the set of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra homomorphisms $\psi : A_N \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\psi(\bar\jmath) = j_0$ is nonempty. Only the existence of such a bijection is asserted, not a particular one.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the places of the affine modular curve $X_0(N)$ minus its cusps and the maximal ideals of its coordinate ring, restricted to the fibre over a given value $j_0$ of the $j$-function. It is used in the counts of the places at which $\bar\jmath$ or $\bar\jmath - 1728$ has order exactly one, which produce the quantities $\nu_3$ and $\nu_2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_nonempty_equiv_place_pos_ord_algHom_integralClosure.lean

